    {
      "kind": "TEXTBOX",
      "characters": 288,
      "text": "The energy eigenvalues of the pairing model Hamiltonian can be extracted using the quantum phase estimation algorithm. The second-quantized Hamiltonian is transformed into qubits and then into quantum gates. The entire quantum computation is outlined, from the Hamiltonian to measurement."
    },
    {
      "kind": "TEXTBOX",
      "characters": 712,
      "text": "where U is a unitary matrix, which can be arbitrarily approximated by a universal set of gates such as CNOT, H, and T. To create the controlled-U gate shown above, one can decompose the unitary into\n                     where\n\n\n\n\nand\n\n\nis a rotation about the Q = X, Y, Z axis on the Bloch sphere. First we prepare an initial state     ,which can be expanded in terms of the eigenvectors of the Hamiltonian. By implementing the given quantum circuit and measuring the top n gates, one will obtain the phase as a binary fraction. The correct phases will be obtained with the highest probability. One must repeat this process several times in order to determine the probability distribution of the obtained phases."
    },
